## Why This Is Asked
Gauges how well a candidate designs feature-level gating in a per-user scoring API, a practical knob for privacy, performance, and experimentation.

## Key Concepts
- Feature gating: filter features at the API boundary.
- Deterministic scoring: gating should not introduce nondeterminism.
- Validation & observability: log gating decisions for audits.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply feature gating before scoring
function computeScoreWithGating(allFeatures, allowedFeatures){
  const mask = new Set(allowedFeatures || allFeatures.map(f => f.name));
  const included = allFeatures.filter(f => mask.has(f.name));
  return computeScoreFromFeatures(included);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to validate and handle invalid feature names?
- How would you scale gating across multiple model_versions?

## Why This Is Asked
Schema evolution is common in production systems. This tests ability to plan backward-compatible changes that don’t break existing clients.

## Key Concepts
- API versioning and data contracts
- Migration scripts and defaulting
- Feature flags and canary rollouts
- Regression and contract tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Migration mapping
function migrate(payload) {
  if (payload.score_source) return payload;
  if (payload.model_version >= 2) payload.score_source = 'model';
  else payload.score_source = 'heuristic';
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback a failed migration?
- Which tests best validate both old and new clients?
